{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2134","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Permutation Oddness"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given four positive integers $$$c_0$$$, $$$c_1$$$, $$$c_2$$$, and $$$c_3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$n = c_0 + c_1 + c_2 + c_3$$$. Consider an array $$$a$$$ of $$$n$$$ integers with $$$x$$$ ($$$0\\le x\\le 3$$$) appearing $$$c_x$$$ times. For any "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"distinct permutation"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ $$$b$$$ of the array $$$a$$$, define its "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"oddness"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" as$$$^{\\text{†}}$$$$$$^{\\text{‡}}$$$:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$\\sum_{i = 1}^{n-1} \\text{lowbit}(b_i \\oplus b_{i+1})$$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to count, for each integer $$$k$$$ from $$$0$$$ to $$$2 \\cdot (n-1)$$$ (inclusive), the number of distinct permutations of $$$a$$$ with an oddness equal to $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Since the numbers might be too large, you are only required to find them modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$A permutation of the array is an arrangement of its elements into any order. For example, $$$[1,2,2]$$$ is a permutation of $$$[2,2,1]$$$, but $$$[1,1,2]$$$ is not. Two permutations are considered distinct if they differ in at least one position."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{†}}$$$$$$\\oplus$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{‡}}$$$$$$\\text{lowbit}(x)$$$ is the value of the lowest binary bit of $$$x$$$, e.g. $$$\\text{lowbit}(12)=4$$$, $$$\\text{lowbit}(8)=8$$$. Specifically, we define $$$\\text{lowbit}(0) = 0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 50$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and the only line of each test case contains four positive integers $$$c_0$$$, $$$c_1$$$, $$$c_2$$$, and $$$c_3$$$ ($$$1 \\le c_0, c_1, c_2, c_3 \\lt 800$$$, $$$4 \\le c_0 + c_1 + c_2 + c_3 \\le 800$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$n = c_0 + c_1 + c_2 + c_3$$$. It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$800$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output $$$2 \\cdot (n-1) + 1$$$ integers in one line — the number of distinct permutations of $$$a$$$ with an oddness equal to $$$0,1,\\ldots, 2 \\cdot (n-1)$$$ respectively. Output the answers modulo $$$10^9+7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1 1 1 1\n1 2 4 1\n3 3 3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0 0 0 8 8 8 0\n0 0 0 8 32 126 184 244 156 72 18 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 8 56 424 1472 5760 12128 29376 40384 65232 59920 65232 40384 29376 12128 5760 1472 424 56 8 0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the array $$$a$$$ has $$$24$$$ distinct permutations. The table below shows the oddness values for some selected permutations:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Permutation"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Oddness"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[0,1,2,3]$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\text{lowbit}(0 \\oplus 1) + \\text{lowbit}(1 \\oplus 2) + \\text{lowbit}(2 \\oplus 3) = 1 + 1 + 1 = 3$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[0,2,1,3]$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\text{lowbit}(0 \\oplus 2) + \\text{lowbit}(2 \\oplus 1) + \\text{lowbit}(1 \\oplus 3) = 2 + 1 + 2 = 5$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[0,1,3,2]$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$\\text{lowbit}(0 \\oplus 1) + \\text{lowbit}(1 \\oplus 3) + \\text{lowbit}(3 \\oplus 2) = 1 + 2 + 1 = 4$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall, among the $$$24$$$ permutations:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$8$$$ permutations have oddness $$$3$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$8$$$ permutations have oddness $$$4$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$8$$$ permutations have oddness $$$5$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the array $$$a$$$ has $$$840$$$ distinct permutations. The distribution of oddness values is as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$8$$$ permutations have oddness $$$3$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$32$$$ permutations have oddness $$$4$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$126$$$ permutations have oddness $$$5$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$184$$$ permutations have oddness $$$6$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$244$$$ permutations have oddness $$$7$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$156$$$ permutations have oddness $$$8$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$72$$$ permutations have oddness $$$9$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$18$$$ permutations have oddness $$$10$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"2134F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2134/problem/F"}